destroying the world is a Mass Ascension level gambit, and to the best of our knowledge no one has managed one of those yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, Mass Ascension or destroying the world? Because I distinctly remember a Time of Judgment\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T18:01:55-07:00","id":862317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=862221#post862221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, Mass Ascension or destroying the world? Because I distinctly remember a Time of Judgment\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually can't remember, but didn't that include an option for Mass Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:51:29-07:00","id":862481,"title":"","content":"Yep. It sure did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T02:43:56-07:00","id":862534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=862481#post862481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. It sure did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could have spared us of it, though. Ascension really wasn't very well thought out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T04:40:07-07:00","id":863106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi#post858849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Almost finished the Mage 20, and been loving almost all of it. The idea of so many everyday actions - such as putting on perfume before a meeting - being actual rituals, is fantastic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ALMOST all of it. Do you think there are many humans who simultaneously have all the following qualities:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1) They are suicidal, seeking their own destruction and that of the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2) They think over the long term.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3) They are highly disciplined, discrete, and good at hiding their own personality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4) They are immune to social pressure from those they interact with day after day after day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">5) They are wantonly sadistic and enjoy the suffering of others.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">6) They coordinate perfectly with each other, and have an efficient hierarchy that disseminates information and instructions while leaving minimal traces. This means they have minimal infighting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">7) They are mages, so filled with hubris and arrogance.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And so, the Nephandi fail for me. Big time. Finding one suicidal-planner-discreet-disciplined-sadistic-bureaucratic-hubristic person might be possible, or a small group, but a whole faction? We should believe that, alone of any large groups of humans throughout history, ones who have solved the whole &quot;efficient organisation with minimal overhead&quot; problem are the self-destructive devil worshippers? If you think of them as human beings with their own twisted wants and agendas, ask yourself &quot;what makes them work together better than any other group&quot;?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think a real world group that would hit most of these marks would be &quot;high-functioning sociopaths.&quot; While I am pretty sure these are pretty rare in reality, 1) this is the World of Darkness so there are going to be more of them, and as others have pointed out, 2) the cauls help quite a bit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T04:46:25-07:00","id":863570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=862221#post862221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, Mass Ascension or destroying the world? Because I distinctly remember a Time of Judgment\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>That was just a mass hallucination. Mention of the event is against Technocracy Protocols. Report to Room 101 for reconditioning to the new truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T05:41:35-07:00","id":863581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=862219#post862219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is, however, a term for at least three different factions of evil mages who've mortgaged their souls/been remade by different masters and thus should have different ultimate goals whose main common characteristic is &quot;evil with a capital E.&quot; Hell's win condition is not the same as that of Malfeas, which is (probably) not the same as that of the Outer Dark, which may in fact have multiple competing agendas as varied as the sanity-blasting horrors that lurk in it. That setup continued to be the case from First Edition through Revised, and I'm not aware of it changing with M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serving different masters? Possibly, although M20's comments on Nephandi 'service' are one of the few things I like from that chapter. But is there any indication that the Cauls are substantively different based on who is running them? I'm not sure the Avatar is so easy to manipulate that custom soul surgery is available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's always been a contradiction between the organizing structures of the Nephandi and the unifying principle developers have been assigning to them since 2nd Edition. </div> </div> </div>I'm getting images of the four major factions in a group therapy session trying to deal with all of the contradictions the writers have inflicted. The Technocracy is saying: &quot;You think you have problems. We used to have control over reality and cool black hats, even. Then they decided technology wasn't evil, and then the reorgs and the memos. It's getting so I have to open the GttTech to find out if I'm supposed to torture prisoners today.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T06:39:46-07:00","id":863599,"title":"","content":"There's something to that. My understanding is that Phil reimagined the Nephandi for M20 based on a personal experience he had with a girl who manipulated him. So M20's Nephandi are much more conniving bastards who get off on corrupting those who think they're immune to such corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T04:46:22-07:00","id":864208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=863599#post863599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something to that. My understanding is that Phil reimagined the Nephandi for M20 based on a personal experience he had with a girl who manipulated him. So M20's Nephandi are much more conniving bastards who get off on corrupting those who think they're immune to such corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot more sense than it should. There are one or two people I've known who inform my thoughts on Nephandi too, both in how they acted and in how they made the others around them feel about themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:54:33-07:00","id":864241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=863599#post863599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something to that. My understanding is that Phil reimagined the Nephandi for M20 based on a personal experience he had with a girl who manipulated him. So M20's Nephandi are much more conniving bastards who get off on corrupting those who think they're immune to such corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a source for this? It wouldn't be the first time that real life informed art, but it does sound like something personal enough for the Author not to share willy nilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:08:42-07:00","id":864332,"title":"","content":"An interview he had while he was writing M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:01:43-07:00","id":885614,"title":"","content":"Like I mentioned in another thread, the nephandi concept makes me unease and they seem only a crappy bogeymen to be hated by all, a black and white villain, something that doesn't exist in reality and something that is very out of tone with the rest of the Mage philosophy. How can someone be evil, absolute evil, in a world formed by competing paradigms? They should just represent another paradigm, as valuable and objective as the others, but they don't represent any paradigm, even their objectives don't make sense. In one scenario they are bent on preventing Voormas from killing death and are just cannon fodder, in the other they enslave humanity to demon alien lords, etc.. Does this mean that all evil mages in the cWoD are automatically nephandi, specially viewing through the lenses of contemporary morals? Are technocrats and euthanatos nephandi? Are verbena who sacrificed peasants in druidic grooves, nephandi?<br /> <br /> On top of being a disciplined, discreet, nihilistic yet suicidal group, as OP mentioned, they also can alter mage avatars forever, they can steal people's freewill forever, they can make people be a nephandus even if they die and incarnate in another life. It's simply setting breaking. It's like in Buffy the vampire slayer when people lose their souls when becoming vampires: it doesn't matter the people they kill, torture and feed from! They lost their souls, free will and moral compass. ;-) Such convenient villains, the moral scapegoats.<br /> <br /> The only interesting way to insert nephandi in a game it's either make player characters question the evil within (ie, if they were nephandi in another life and their actions were an all orchestrated plot by their inverted avatars) or if you make it seem as if the nephandi are in the end right and all other factions are misguided, something very plausible considering how the nephandi are efficient as an organization.<br /> <br /> My explanation for the nephandi creation is that Mage devs come from a 90's and early 00's american context and have problems understanding fascist/third way movements that happened in history. They probably consider spanish falangism, italian fascism, just irrational and corrupted aberrations, exactly the things they attribute to nephandi. It's no surprise that world war 2 and nazi germany in the cWoD are nephandic events, and make absolutely no magickal or political sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:37:14-07:00","id":885649,"title":"","content":"If any faction in the WoD had any sort of cohesion the setting wouldnt be the delightful clusterfornication that we love. If even the the technocracy were united in the modern age they could kick over the rest of the nightfolk with ease. But they bicker. Argue over method and get in one anothers way. <br /> The same goes with the nephandi. Just because you seek descent doesnt mean your friend Edgelord McGee is going to agree. You might decide descent is when grandmother rises and consumes the lie that is the light. Edgelord McGee however wants to rip up the astral plane and scatter all the foolish constructs of humankinds lie of existance to the edge of the abyss. Both are driven by their avatar to rip it all down, but like all magi they filter this drive through their fradgile humaun mind and THAT is where things get so confused. Edgelord McGee is right. You are right. The technocracy is right. Even the marauders are right because the true purple secret to reality is that humans tell it what to be. Maybe we aren't meant to see behind the curtain but the awakened do, and only like, five agree on what they see there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T22:42:50-07:00","id":885972,"title":"","content":"One thing that really bothers me:<br /> It says that there are two kinds of Nephandi: the Barabbi and the Widderslainte.<br /> However...what about the former non-Awakened Pawns who Awakened after/during when they went into a Caul?<br /> Or those that Awakened with a Nephandic paradigm on their own (through being either acolytes or consors, for example. Or totally on their own, like a dark version of an Orphan) and then went into a Caul? (or maybe this type wouldn't really have to go through a Caul, much like it's noted in the case of the Widderslaintes)<br /> <br /> Whether we would count this as one extra type of Nephandi or two, this still seems extremely distinct from those Barabbi Nephandi who are former members of other Magickal paradigms. I'd say they warrant a separate considerations when describing the Nephandi, separate from the Barabbi. M20 says outright: <i>&quot;The barabbi began along a different Path but then converted to the Nephandic cause. Traitors to their original sects (...)&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> A principal example of such persons would be non-Awakened leaders of successful cults (be they Infernal, Wyrmish or K'llashaa). Upon being contacted by the Nephandi and potentially Awakening, they in all likelihood find fitting in extremely easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=863599#post863599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something to that. My understanding is that Phil reimagined the Nephandi for M20 based on a personal experience he had with a girl who manipulated him. So M20's Nephandi are much more conniving bastards who get off on corrupting those who think they're immune to such corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspiration for the Decadenti, perhaps?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=858960#post858960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">K'llashaa are essentially lovecraftian terrors from beyond space-time. All tentacles, chaos, insanity and primordial power. Their Nephandi would essentially be like the servants of Azhatoth or Nyarlathotep. You've also skipped the faction that simply adores the Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the &quot;faction that simply adores the Oblivion&quot; detailed somewhere? Or you mean the &quot;run-of-the-mill&quot; &quot;Just doesn't care...&quot; Nephandi that sometimes gets mentioned in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-04-2017, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T05:16:56-07:00","id":886123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=885972#post885972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that really bothers me:<br /> It says that there are two kinds of Nephandi: the Barabbi and the Widderslainte.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Or those that Awakened with a Nephandic paradigm on their own (through being either acolytes or consors, for example. Or totally on their own, like a dark version of an Orphan) and then went into a Caul? (or maybe this type wouldn't really have to go through a Caul, much like it's noted in the case of the Widderslaintes)<br /> <br /> Whether we would count this as one extra type of Nephandi or two, this still seems extremely distinct from those Barabbi Nephandi who are former members of other Magickal paradigms. I'd say they warrant a separate considerations when describing the Nephandi, separate from the Barabbi. M20 says outright: <i>&quot;The barabbi began along a different Path but then converted to the Nephandic cause. Traitors to their original sects (...)&quot;</i>. Even calling them &quot;Pure Barabbi.&quot; would be a distinct and nice improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Barabbi/Widderslainte distinction isn't meant to cover all the permutations that could lead someone to the Nephandi, it simply covers one simple but profound question that affects everything about the character's story. Did she choose the Fall or was she Fallen from the start? Everything else is a subdivision of one of those two alternatives. I'm sure the Nephandi do have terms for those subdivisions, it does seem like the kind of thing they fight about, but every true Nephandi is either Barabbi or Widderslainte.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=885972#post885972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A principal example of such persons would be non-Awakened leaders of successful cults (be they Infernal, Wyrmish or K'llashaa). Upon being contacted by the Nephandi and potentially Awakening, they in all likelihood find fitting in extremely easy...&quot;You mean I have to go to this..Caul in order be truly worthy? By all means I shall consider this, but right now I have no time, I have my cult's matters to attend to....and I'd welcome any good advise any of you might have..&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how dark, if they don't have an inverted Avatar, they aren't real Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=885972#post885972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However...what about the former non-Awakened Pawns who Awakened after/during when they went into a Caul?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never actually considered that this could happen, and I would say that the default assumption is that it doesn't. You have to choose the Cauls or you die, and I doubt a Sleeper has the context to make that choice. That said, it would be a hell of a story idea if one Nephandic group was trying to mass produce Widderslainte by indoctrinating children to accept the cauls and then sacrificing them so the twisted Avatar could emerge elsewhere. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T05:17:34-07:00","id":886124,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure where you're getting this concept of non-awakened Nephandi. You need to be a True Mage to actually go into the Caul, There is a world of difference between a mortal cultist (with investments or fomordom) and a True Mage. There is no &quot;Nephandic Paradigm&quot; to awaken to. It's all about philosiphy and what you do, not about some arbitrary new magical belief system that you get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T00:00:52-07:00","id":913923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi#post858849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Almost finished the Mage 20, and been loving almost all of it. The idea of so many everyday actions - such as putting on perfume before a meeting - being actual rituals, is fantastic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ALMOST all of it. Do you think there are many humans who simultaneously have all the following qualities:</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that with recent social... how do you call it? pressure? awareness? tightened policy? developers choose to thread on the safe road and avoid giving protagonists any traits that could attract scandal or social outrage. Euthanatos? No longer death mages. Technocracy atrocities? Devil made them do it. Mages exploiting mortals? Corruption Immanent.<br /> A pity, i liked the grittier older version more. Dark Triad tho... love that merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 06-14-2016, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:15:02-07:00","id":914445,"title":"","content":"I wasn't a fan of the whole 'there are no entities the Nephandi serve' personally. I preferred the 3 general divisions presented in the Book of Madness where you had the infernalists who serve demons, devils, and other hellish entities (example Nergali Baali); the servants of the Wyrm and Maeljin Incarna(examples Pentex, Black Spiral Dancers); and the servants to the Outsiders (example K'llasshaa). While these groups have some similarities each of their end games prevent long term cooperation as they are mutually exclusive; the various infernal entities want to make reality into hell and rule it, the Wyrm servants want to destroy reality, and the Outsiders want to return to reality and alter it to fit their alien whims. Even within one group you end up with divisions over methodology; for example Black Spiral Dancers refuse to work with the Maeljin Incarna, differing infernal entities and their cults will fight for the right to rule (the Outsiders are simply not developed enough in White Wolf to tell what kind of divisions exist although I imagine it would be similar to the issues that affect infernal entities). This all leads to each group of Nephandi being somewhat unique with its own particular feel based on which group they align with which I think makes a better foe than a generic monolithic Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T00:40:19-07:00","id":922494,"title":"","content":"If it's any consolation, I actually did my own variant of the Nephandi which worked very well:<br /> <br /> <b>Cyclical Nephandi</b><br /> <br /> The majority of Nephandi are merely broken shattered shells of former people. They hate the world, they hate the universe, they hate themselves, and they hate everyone else. Cyclical Nephandi are this, certainly, but they have an ideology which unites them in more than the psychopathic spiral of destruction which all other Nephandi seem to aspire to. Many Traditionalists don't actually believe Cyclical Nephandi qualify for the moniker despite going through the Cauls and being as passionately devoted to the destruction of everything as other Nephandus because, well, the idea of them having an ideology beyond destruction goes against the purpose of what a Nephandi is all about, doesn't it? To many, they are simply spectacularly evil mages and may even have a warped form of Ascension planned.<br /> <br /> The Cyclical Nephandi argue, in fact, they are the true Nephandus and that all other examples of their kind are merely Infernalists or people suffering a cosmic temper tantrum. They are a cooler kind of malevolence and quite proud of their calm, methodical pursuit of oblivion for reality. So, in simple terms, what is the Cyclical Nephandi ideology?<br /> <br /> <i>This world is wrong.</i><br /> <br /> This is certainly an attitude most mages can get behind. It is the basis for the Ascension War in fact. Cyclical Nephandi, however, take it to a larger extent. The world is not just wrong, it is a prison and there is absolutely nothing wrong saving in. Why have death? Why have the Shadowlands? Why have a human race which could CONCEIVE of something like this World of Darkness and then believe in it enough to create it? Why value a race which seems to have won the Ascension War from the Union and Traditions by choosing aggressive ignorance in the face of hope? Cyclical Nephandi have a Gnostic view of the world which does not necessarily believe there is anything better beyond this reality but that since mages are divine entities that they could undoubtedly make something better if it wasn't weighed down by all the garbage of the universe.<br /> <br /> It is not enough for Cyclical Nephandi to kill everyone (though many think that would help), that would just leave a world full of Wraiths or Trapped avatars. No, they have to UNMAKE reality so that it never existed. Only then can the Pure Ones reassemble or the mages can be freed to their true potential or, simply, something else emerge from the void better than the failed experiment which is humanity.<br /> <br /> The scary thing is they're not necessarily wrong as if the world as is, is destroyed, a suitably powerful mage could make a new one in its place without the cosmic detritus of the current broken system. A broken vase can never be fixed perfectly so why not just forge a new one? Or simply accept life is a failed experiment with no point? Let the spirits replace mankind or sweet release from all things? These are the subject of spirited debates among the Cyclical Nephandus.<br /> <br /> What, if anything, will replace mankind when it and all of its works are swept away is something there is often disagreement about but it is not THIS. So they can work together toward the destruction of everything. All they need is the Cauls to remove any pesky conscience or hesitation to doing what they need to do. It gives them a purity of thought and purpose which would make them pity other mages if they still had that in them.<br /> <br /> Cyclical Nephanus are servants of the Abyss, Oblivion, and the cosmic force of Entropy without Renewal. Some are interested in physical eradication of the world and work to foster war, conflict, and destruction. Others are interested in a spiritual destruction of the world, one soul at a time, leading mortals to not want to live on. Others hope to break down reality's barriers so Oblivion consumes this universe entirety. A great majority believe mankind unconsciously wishes for death already and the slow march to extinction will result in the Mass Consensus eradicating itself. To win, the Cyclical Nephandi do not have to achieve their goal.<br /> <br /> They simply have to make the other Traditions and Technocrats and Dreamers do not.<br /> <br /> And they're doing a great job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-29-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:44:22-07:00","id":923495,"title":"","content":"Now that's an interesting opponent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:49:48-07:00","id":923500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=923495#post923495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that's an interesting opponent...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar problem with the Nephandi as I consider Mage a game of competing philosophies. For me, the Nephandi should be able to articulate why someone should want to eradicate the universe and give a coherent idea of their philosophy. Given the nature of Gnosticism and the fact reality is fundamentally &quot;fake&quot; in M:TA I always felt there was a missed opportunity for Nephandi to be the guys saying, &quot;Okay, if reality is created by will then it's all a big illusion so let's end the illusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> It would sound insane but under the right circumstances, it might sound coherent.<br /> <br /> Also, if you knew God was either nonexistent or the product of deranged beliefs of fundamentalists then you might want to remake the world with a better one (perhaps you). You just have to get rid of the current reality.<br /> <br /> You know, give the Nephandi a point (if a crazy one).<br /> <br /> I admit I was partially inspired by the Thalmor, who have a coherent but batshit philosophy as to why unmaking reality is a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:13:54-07:00","id":923514,"title":"","content":"The way I played it in my <b><i>big</i></b> Mage game a decade ago, is that Nephandi (or at least, the first generation of them) were originally a conspiracy of Entropic mages who realized destruction is an inevitable part of the great cycle, and that without Entropy the Tellurian would simply reside in perpetual Stasis, which to them of all potential outcomes was the <i>worst</i>, particularly for the fact they extrapolated that Paradox is inextricably linked to Stasis, and the opposite and equal to Quintessence. They saw the rise of Stasis as the death of True Magick -- not just for Traditions and Crafts, but even for the Order of Reason. So, to avoid this outcome, they decided to see to it the Tellurian received the Good Death as quickly and painlessly as possible, to spare not only mages but sleepers an infinity of mere, hopeless existence.<br /> <br /> And yes, in that game the Chakravanti were the originating point of the Nephandi, and from whom that viewpoint expanded to other societies of mages. Needless to say, a group of death mages evangelizing the end of the world as a way to forestall the death of True Magick (even though this very philosophy is what fully half the world's mages believed in <i>anyways</i>) <i>wasn't</i> taken well by other mages...and they ended up facing some <i><b>catastrophically</b></i> bad press.<br /> <br /> Then (in a self-fulfilling prophecy), like the Chakravanti before them, they started succumbing to Jhor, worshiping alien powers, inverting their Avatars, and the rest was history. They invented the idea of Descent, and the like. Making them more akin to really, <b><i>really</i></b> misguided Marauders than anything else, really. So, the original &quot;true&quot; Nephandi quietly rejoined the Chakravanti, slipping their own beliefs and teachings in with the Traditions' innate Buddhist, Hindu, and Zoroastrian philosophies, creating the Euthanatoi -- forging a Tradition uniquely trained and positioned to combat the <i>fallen</i> Nephandi while normalizing their own beliefs the Tellurian would eventually need to end so that it may be reborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:31:29-07:00","id":923528,"title":"","content":"That's an awesome origin Theodrim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T00:50:54-07:00","id":923751,"title":"","content":"I never quite got why the Nephandi always get the blanket coverage of 'They want to unmake everything' in some parts of the books.<br /> <br /> If you read the descriptions of the individual Nephandi factions..that's quite simply not true for most of them.<br /> <br /> * The &quot;Cthulhu&quot; Nephandi serving the beings from the Deep Umbra do not want to unmake reality - They want to weaken Earth and Humanity so those dark beings can reclaim what they percieve as their dominion and domination. They percieve Humanity as rising up bunch of strangely powerful young beings that need squashing. And the Nephandi are probably promised all sorts of things in return. They probably got twisted and inverted, cthulhu-style, by those otherworldly beings. None of these beings plan to erase the Tellurian itself.<br /> <br /> * The Infernal Nephandi get into pacts with devils and demons, initially lusting for power or getting suckered into sweet deals, or being offered a 'helping' hand in their desparation...and thus begins the downward spiral of utter corruption and demise. They are not even inherently evil at start. They do not even necessarily have their sights set on other mages at all. Until they finally twisted and inverted by these infernal demons. None of these beings plan to erase the Tellurian either. Most of the demons simply use those Nephandi to pull more people into damnation, while delighting in the evental demise of the Nephandus.<br /> <br /> * The Malfeas/Wyrm Nephandi - Here we go. <i>These</i> are the guys that want to unmake everything, and are the kind of Nephandus that seemingly most often is associated with the overall term Nephandus. These guys want to end <i>everything</i>, and they got twisted and warped by the cauls/Labyrinths. Literal Widderslante are probably exclusive to these.<br /> <br /> And yes, I also never got why *<i>all</i>* factions of Nephandi supposedly go through the cauls - the wyrm/malfea associated Nephandi do. But as I stated above...it does not make sense for the other factions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I *like* the idea of the Cyclical Nephandi as stated by CTPhipps, but I am not even sure they can be called Nephandi - I don't see why their avatars should have gotten inverted in the first place.<br /> <br /> And remember, that's what actually makes a Nephandus a Nephandus: The avatar inversion. Evil, <i>corrupted</i> avatars, not necessarily evil, corrupted people...at least at first. You can only stay normal with a corrupt Avatar for so long.<br /> Heck, you can have utterly evil a-hole Mages that like to headbutt babies before eating them, but that does <b>not</b> make them a Nephandus - the avatar inversion runs a little deeper than being just an evil person. It means having an utterly corrupted avatar. (Even uninverted Avatars can be plain <i>ruthless</i> and amoral. Not the same thing.)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Cyclical 'Nephandi' ( IMO, CTPhipps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) are just a conspiracy of Mages that seek to end the Tellurian's corruption and suffering in a way they think is right - if utterly radical. <i>There is nothing 'corrupt' about them</i>. Of course the Traditions and Technocrats will still treat them like Nephandi.<br /> ..and the Malfean Nephandi are probably having a field day infiltrating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-30-2016, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:16:51-07:00","id":923765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=923751#post923751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never quite got why the Nephandi always get the blanket coverage of 'They want to unmake everything' in some parts of the books.<br /> <br /> If you read the descriptions of the individual Nephandi factions..that's quite simply not true for most of them.<br /> <br /> * The &quot;Cthulhu&quot; Nephandi serving the beings from the Deep Umbra do not want to unmake reality - They want to weaken Earth and Humanity so those dark beings can reclaim what they percieve as their dominion and domination. They percieve Humanity as rising up bunch of strangely powerful young beings that need squashing. And the Nephandi are probably promised all sorts of things in return. They probably got twisted and inverted, cthulhu-style, by those otherworldly beings. None of these beings plan to erase the Tellurian itself.<br /> <br /> * The Infernal Nephandi get into pacts with devils and demons, initially lusting for power or getting suckered into sweet deals, or being offered a 'helping' hand in their desparation...and thus begins the downward spiral of utter corruption and demise. They are not even inherently evil at start. They do not even necessarily have their sights set on other mages at all. Until they finally twisted and inverted by these infernal demons. None of these beings plan to erase the Tellurian either. Most of the demons simply use those Nephandi to pull more people into damnation, while delighting in the evental demise of the Nephandus.<br /> <br /> * The Malfeas/Wyrm Nephandi - Here we go. <i>These</i> are the guys that want to unmake everything, and are the kind of Nephandus that seemingly most often is associated with the overall term Nephandus. These guys want to end <i>everything</i>, and they got twisted and warped by the cauls/Labyrinths. Literal Widderslante are probably exclusive to these.<br /> <br /> And yes, I also never got why *<i>all</i>* factions of Nephandi supposedly go through the cauls - the wyrm/malfea associated Nephandi do. But as I stated above...it does not make sense for the other factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I think the answer to that is the Nephandus are meant to be Daleks. Basically, they exist for the explicit purpose of giving the PCs something which they can blow up and engage with their magic without any of the moral philosophizing or naval gazing which accompanies, well, just about every discussion of the Technocracy vs. Traditions.<br /> <br /> They're meant to be comic book evil I think rather than something which is really thought out on a coherent thematic level. Why do the Nephandi want to put demon blood in children's toys which will kill them all ala Halloween 3? Well, because they're evil. Why do they want to collect souls? Evil. Why do they want to launch all the nuclear weapons in the world with a Paradox-less rite? EVIL!<br /> <br /> Which is ironic because the Doctor naval gazes over the Daleks and their existence all the time. Likewise, the Cauls actually caused many interesting discussions among my PCs. &quot;What does this mean for the humans attached to a Nephandus avatar? Can they be blamed for their crimes? If magic can do anything. why not heal avatars? Should they be contained instead?&quot; You know, good old fashioned RPGing.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I changed the nature of the Cauls so they don't actually automatically make you a monster but just constantly tempt you to do evil and try to warp your magic.<br /> <br /> It led to a fun campaign where a PC had a Nephandus Avatar which was basically just constantly advising them to be a supervillain and they had to hide it while the cabal looked for a cure. The campaign ended on a good note when after purifying it with a player voluntarily sacrificing themselves, they ended up having to have her embraced (destroying her forever) because the Nephandi were about ready to drag her back and torture her into compliance.<br /> <br /> Good campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I *like* the idea of the Cyclical Nephandi as stated by CTPhipps, but I am not even sure they can be called Nephandi - I don't see why their avatars should have gotten inverted in the first place.<br /> <br /> And remember, that's what actually makes a Nephandus a Nephandus: The avatar inversion. Evil, <i>corrupted</i> avatars, not necessarily evil, corrupted people...at least at first. You can only stay normal with a corrupt Avatar for so long.<br /> Heck, you can have utterly evil a-hole Mages that like to headbutt babies before eating them, but that does <b>not</b> make them a Nephandus - the avatar inversion runs a little deeper than being just an evil person. It means having an utterly corrupted avatar. (Even uninverted Avatars can be plain <i>ruthless</i> and amoral. Not the same thing.)<br /> <br /> The Cyclical 'Nephandi' ( IMO, CTPhipps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) are just a conspiracy of Mages that seek to end the Tellurian's corruption and suffering in a way they think is right - if utterly radical. <i>There is nothing 'corrupt' about them</i>. Of course the Traditions and Technocrats will still treat them like Nephandi.<br /> ..and the Malfean Nephandi are probably having a field day infiltrating them. </div> </div> </div>Thanks, glad you liked them. As for the avatar inversion, I think my argument was the Cyclical Nephandi went through the rite to make sure future generations of their avatar would have the same inclination to burn the universe down in order to free it. Then again, that was the point of them to make a coherent (if utterly <i>insane</i> to anyone <b>but</b> a mage) argument while still being evil to the core.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the Baali in Clanbook: Baali or the villains of <i>The Cabin in the Woods</i>. They have a justification which they can articulate even if it doesn't justify what they do.<br /> <br /> I will also freely admit while the Cyclical Nephandi are good for a conversation, it's also nice just to have evil psychopaths out to do nasty deeds when you need a quick adventure too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:43:37-07:00","id":923771,"title":"","content":"I respectfully disagree with CTPhipps, as I view the various Nephandi philosophies as being a front from a significantly more irrational reason: they just want to corrupt, despoil, and destroy. It's hard-coded into them, and informs their actions on an emotional level. Everything else is after-the-fact rationalization.<br /> <br /> Personally I think it makes sense. All regular Mages are driven towards Ascension by their Avatars, and said Avatars don't necessarily care about <i>what </i>the Mage believes. They just want the Mage to ascend. It's a positive, not necessarily philosophical goal. It's more primal, these positivist emotional urges towards becoming better.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are the direct opposite. Their inverted Avatars want Descent, and fill the Nephandus's heart with hate, bitterness, and sadistic desire. And such an Avatar is created by a conscious decision by the Mage (in at least one of their incarnations) to reject positivism and embrace negativism. To forsake Hope in favor of Despair.<br /> <br /> This possibility would actually justify the different factions of Nephandi, and their apparent inconsistent motivations. It's not that the Nephandi want to destroy creation...they just hate it. Their hearts are filled with foul black ichor, driving them towards atavistic violence - or violation - against anything and everything around them. Different groups, obviously, have different ideas about how they ought to express that hatred. The Malfeans are, of course, all about annihilation. They've jumped straight to Oblivion and see that as the only true way to sate their urge to purge. The Infernalists aren't quite so suicidal, but would be happy seeing the world turned into a new wing of Hell (hopefully with them promoted to cushy positions as reward for their loyalty). And the unpronounceable ones want the Great Ones to free them to revel and kill, and teach them new ways to revel and kill. A desire for unfettered wickedness, blended with a heavy dose of cosmic madness.<br /> <br /> And then you have independent Nephandi - the ones who think the others are stupid for tying themselves to demonic patrons - who want to see the world burn on their own terms. Unfortunately, that means also not having big, cosmic powers to lend a hand to their schemes. They retain their freedom, but by that token remain handicapped in other ways. <hr /><br /> Lately, the question of how the Nephandi first came into existence has bugged me. What I've been going with, after some thought, is based on a sometimes mentioned idea in the books, about Nephandi whose Avatars inverted without going to the Cauls. And this being accomplished by the Mage's mind being so filled with negative emotions, that they essentially went through a Caul of the heart. Without assistance by an evil labyrinth, they just...auto-Fall, by shear force of despair.<br /> <br /> (Come to think of it, this is not unlike how Witches are created in Puella Magi Madoka Magica...).<br /> <br /> My theory about where the Nephandi come from is simply that, in the deepest depths of history, this scenario happened for the first time with a Mage. Maybe the Pure Ones had left by this point, or maybe the actions of this newly Fallen Mage were the reason they were toppled in the first place. Whatever the case, you had a Mage so dark, so wrong-minded, that they twisted themself into becoming an enemy of creation. Maybe this Mage - through multiple incarnations perhaps - met others who had experienced the same Fall, and banded together. Or maybe he or she was alone for the longest time, and &quot;wanted company&quot;. Whatever the case, this Nephandus and possibly others worked to find a way to engineer the inversion of Avatars.<br /> <br /> Hence, the creation of the first Cauls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 06-30-2016, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:49:30-07:00","id":924396,"title":"","content":"Relevant to the discussion: Negative utilitarianism (in brief: life is suffering, suffering is bad, we should end all life) and the often altruistic and kind people that follow it: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negative_utilitarianism\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negative_utilitarianism</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:43:02-07:00","id":924426,"title":"","content":"Unmaking the Tellurian as an act of mery!<br /> Now that sounds nephandic...<br /> \u201cI am not evil, I am with the good guys! Would you please hand me the doomsday device over there?\u201c<br /> <br /> As expected, every human needs to believe to be good. A smart inverted avatar takes this into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T11:41:19-07:00","id":924553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=924426#post924426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unmaking the Tellurian as an act of mery!<br /> Now that sounds nephandic...<br /> \u201cI am not evil, I am with the good guys! Would you please hand me the doomsday device over there?\u201c<br /> <br /> As expected, every human needs to believe to be good. A smart inverted avatar takes this into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. Just because you can say WHY you do something, doesn't mean it's valid.<br /> <br /> I understand the appeal of making Nephandi the antithesis of Mage's usual philosophy so it's like, &quot;These guys got nothing but badness&quot; but I think it's better to have something like the Sabbat or Union versus Pentex.<br /> <br /> &quot;I get what these guys are getting out of it, even if I think they're nuts.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:02:58-07:00","id":924606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=923751#post923751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never quite got why the Nephandi always get the blanket coverage of 'They want to unmake everything' in some parts of the books.<br /> <br /> If you read the descriptions of the individual Nephandi factions..that's quite simply not true for most of them.<br /> <br /> * The &quot;Cthulhu&quot; Nephandi serving the beings from the Deep Umbra do not want to unmake reality - They want to weaken Earth and Humanity so those dark beings can reclaim what they percieve as their dominion and domination. They percieve Humanity as rising up bunch of strangely powerful young beings that need squashing. And the Nephandi are probably promised all sorts of things in return. They probably got twisted and inverted, cthulhu-style, by those otherworldly beings. None of these beings plan to erase the Tellurian itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I can see some of the Outsider Lords having motivations such as destroying normal reality by consuming it, or being offended by the concept of positive existence and wanting to put a stop to it (kind of like someone with a flashing neon light outside their hotel room window wanting it to go away so they can sleep). I can also see Nephandi that have hitched their wagons to other such beings being so horrified/maddened by their avatar's contact with said masters that they subconsciously want to end the universe to prevent their own cycles of reincarnation from continuing the exposure.<br /> <br /> The infernalists are the real fly in the ointment as far as &quot;destroy everything&quot; being the underlying goal of ALL Nephandi. Almost none of them should be geared toward true nihilism rather than corruption and temptation for their masters' benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:11:36-07:00","id":924610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=924606#post924606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I can see some of the Outsider Lords having motivations such as destroying normal reality by consuming it, or being offended by the concept of positive existence and wanting to put a stop to it (kind of like someone with a flashing neon light outside their hotel room window wanting it to go away so they can sleep). I can also see Nephandi that have hitched their wagons to other such beings being so horrified/maddened by their avatar's contact with said masters that they subconsciously want to end the universe to prevent their own cycles of reincarnation from continuing the exposure.<br /> <br /> The infernalists are the real fly in the ointment as far as &quot;destroy everything&quot; being the underlying goal of ALL Nephandi. Almost none of them should be geared toward true nihilism rather than corruption and temptation for their masters' benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Demon: The Fallen doesn't have Infernals who don't want to end the world. According to Demon: The Fallen, all Demon Lords in Hell want to eradicate everything because they want their pain to stop. The only ones who don't want to are the smaller lesser demons who escaped and have merged with humans. Indeed, even among escaped demons, Raveners are the largest faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:21:49-07:00","id":924615,"title":"","content":"But most Infernalists serve Astral Infernals, who don't seem particularly keen into destroying everything.<br /> <br /> For good or bad, we never got a Mage book that truly delves in Demon: The Fallen and it's own issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:13:18-07:00","id":924746,"title":"","content":"When I was doing Mage fifteen years ago, I found Infernal Sorcerers to be much more interesting than Infernal Nephandi because they had different motivations. Infernal Nephandi want to remake the world so that their masters can come out and play. Infernal Sorcerers want to make a deal and, for better or worse, the Demon Lords were the ones who gave them the best deal. <br /> <br /> Infernal Sorcerers can also be much more common than Infernal Nephandi. I always played with the assumption that the ratio of Mages to Mortals was 1:1,000,000 while the ratio of Sorcerers to Mortals was 1:1,000 (it was based off of my anthropological studies of folk lore and the occult). I figured that the Infernal Nephandi were around 5% of the Mage population (around 360 Mages in 2016 population numbers) and that Infernal Sorcerers were around 5% of the Sorcerer population (around 360,000 Sorcerers in 2016 population numbers).<br /> <br /> Of course, that number of Infernal Sorcerers meant that the good number of millionaires and billionaires in the world were secretly Infernal Sorcerers, but I found that to be acceptable for story purposes. The Infernal Sorcerers were organized into secret societies that were associated with specific Demon Lords, with the average Demon Lord having a few dozen people bound to it. Of course, that meant that the number of human sacrifices every year probably approached 360,000 per year, but a lot of people go missing in the developing world every year, so it was not unreasonable.<br /> <br /> The end result is that the Demon Lords rule the Earth indirectly through their Infernal Sorcerer servants which, while depressing, makes sense considering the state of the world. The elected officials are probably not Infernal Sorcerers, too much public scrutiny, but the majority of the business elite probably are Infernal Sorcerers. They would use their connections and money to influence public policy to fit their masters' agendas but, since there are thousands of Demon Lords, there would be a lot of conflict between groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T23:49:21-07:00","id":924792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=924553#post924553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah. Just because you can say WHY you do something, doesn't mean it's valid.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not, but it can be valid for the Nephandus in question. <br /> Faith and belief in general do not NEED to be validated. <br /> You can go around and tell every practicioner of every Religion that they have no valid argument for their faith, and by extension every mage (except the ones sharing your paradigm of course) also do not have valid arguments for their paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T01:47:56-07:00","id":924820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/858849-my-problem-with-the-nephandi?p=924792#post924792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faith and belief in general do not NEED to be validated. </div> </div> </div> </div>Almost everyone needs social validation, though. Which explains why the Nephandi hang around with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T04:15:54-07:00","id":928681,"title":"","content":"My problem with the M20 Nephandi is that they're written as the ones in &quot;Hell on Earth&quot;, the worst Ascension scenario were - as Villain Sues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1578-patricl_gleason","name":"Patricl_Gleason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1578_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T16:17:19-07:00","id":1490196,"title":"","content":"This is why I vastly prefer the Scelesti of Mage: The Awakening over the Nephandi. I think what is really going on is theme bleed from Werewolf: The Apocalypse. I really, really wish that Mage could be canonically separated from Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T14:34:51-07:00","id":1491240,"title":"","content":"*Sigh*<br /> <br /> Arise, Necro-Thread! Arise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}